CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F496A1775577779
OL,1,  V<,,4<,,4<,,4Spp0pp0p``0pp0      G9/23
OL,2,T]V5b(55b(55j5Sj5.%jj5/l4
OL,3,  V-,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##!
OL,5, Transport Secretary Mr Paul Channon has
OL,6, announced a new package of measures to
OL,7, improve safety on motorways.
OL,8,F
OL,9,FHe stressed that the most important
OL,10,Fpart of the package was "to eliminate
OL,11,Four own bad driving".
OL,12,F
OL,13,FThe measures include mandatory speed
OL,14,Flimits at contraflows and major road-
OL,15,Fworks. Traffic at these sites will
OL,16,Falso be monitored by video equipment.
OL,17,F
OL,18,FIn addition, lorries will normally be
OL,19,Frequired to keep to the nearside lane
OL,20,Fat contraflows, and there will be more
OL,21,Fsigns for the need to change lanes.
OL,22,F
OL,23,T]Cfrom 07-04-88 / teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,497,190,120,250,0,100
PN,49610
SC,0010
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F496A1775577779
OL,1,  V<,,4<,,4<,,4Spp0pp0p``0pp0     G10/23
OL,2,T]V5b(55b(55j5Sj5.%jj5/l4 BACKGROUND
OL,3,  V-,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##! ##########
OL,5, More motorway safety measures announced
OL,6, by the Transport Secretary today:
OL,8,C*FThe often misunderstood "lane closed"
OL,9,Fsignal will be changed to a red cross.
OL,10,F
OL,11,C*FSimilarly, the "restrictions end"
OL,12,Fsign will be replaced by the word "end"
OL,14,C*FDisplays of the most important motor-
OL,15,Fway signs will be arranged at service
OL,16,Fareas. Special motorway safety leaflets
OL,17,Fwill be distributed.
OL,18,F
OL,19,C*FAll learner drivers will be advised
OL,20,Fto take motorway tuition after passing
OL,21,Ftheir test.
OL,22,F
OL,23,T]Cfrom 07-04-88 / teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,497,190,120,250,0,100
PN,49611
SC,0011
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F496A1775577779
OL,1,  V<,,4<,,4<,,4Spp0pp0p``0pp0     G11/23
OL,2,T]V5b(55b(55j5Sj5.%jj5/l4 BACKGROUND
OL,3,  V-,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##! ##########
OL,5, More motorway safety measures announced
OL,6, by the Transport Secretary today:
OL,8,C*FDrivers will have to switch on hazard
OL,9,Flights if at the back of a slow-moving
OL,10,Fqueue.
OL,12,C*FThe possibility of making high centre
OL,13,Fmounted brake lights necessary on new
OL,14,Fvehicles is to be explored.
OL,16,C*FMandatory flammability standards for
OL,17,Fcoach interiors will be introduced.
OL,19,C*FFrom 1990, single-deck coaches will
OL,20,Fhave to have more roof strength; double
OL,21,Fdeckers must have more emergency exits.
OL,22,F
OL,23,T]Cfrom 07-04-88 / teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,497,190,120,250,0,100
PN,49612
SC,0012
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F496A1775577779
OL,1,  V<,,4<,,4<,,4Spp0pp0p``0pp0     G12/23
OL,2,T]V5b(55b(55j5Sj5.%jj5/l4 BACKGROUND
OL,3,  V-,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##! ##########
OL,5, More motorway safety measures announced
OL,6, by the Transport Secretary today:
OL,8,C*FVehicle manufacturers will be asked
OL,9,Fto cut the risk of fires caused by
OL,10,Felectrical components and to fit cut-
OL,11,Foff devices for fuel-injection engines.
OL,13,C*FThe Department of Transport is to
OL,14,Fconsider arrangements for a new driver
OL,15,Flicensing system for 1991.
OL,17,C*FThere will be an experiment on the M1
OL,18,Fto see whether the installation of
OL,19,F70mph signs helps drivers keep within
OL,20,Fthe speed limit.
OL,22,F
OL,23,T]Cfrom 07-04-88 / teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
