CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F496A1775577779
OL,1,  V<,,4<,,4<,,4Spp0pp0p``0pp0     G13/23
OL,2,T]V5b(55b(55j5Sj5.%jj5/l4
OL,3,  V-,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##!
OL,5, The annual conference of Britain's
OL,6, second-largest teachers' union has been
OL,7, told that teachers are coming under
OL,8, increasing stress in the classroom.
OL,9,F
OL,10,FDelegates from the National Association
OL,11,Fof Schoolmasters and Women Teachers
OL,12,Fblamed disruptive pupils and increasing
OL,13,Fworkloads.
OL,15,FThe Government's education policies
OL,16,Fwere also to blame, the Blackpool
OL,17,Fconference was told.
OL,19,FThe problem is causing many more
OL,20,Fstress-related illnesses among teachers
OL,21,Fdelegates said.
OL,22,F
OL,23,T]Cfrom 07-04-88 / teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
